[{:db/id 17592186495046 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c993b31b-1739-52ac-a2f5-55deea55eaf7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c993b31b-1739-52ac-a2f5-55deea55eaf7" :question/id #uuid "c993b31b-1739-52ac-a2f5-55deea55eaf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-68863" :question/problem "Jack bought a pumpkin that weighed $3$ kilograms. The retail price of pumpkin at the store is  $$1.78/kg.$ How much did  Jack pay for the pumpkin?" :question/worked-solution "The unit price of pumpkin is $$1.78/kg.$ To find the cost of  $3$ kilograms of pumpkin, we multiply:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1.78\\times 3 & =5.34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Jack paid  $$5.34$ for the $3$-$\\text{kg}$ pumpkin." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-62ea6bc2-70ac-5760-9ddc-ebf3b618c556"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-62ea6bc2-70ac-5760-9ddc-ebf3b618c556" :answer-field/id #uuid "62ea6bc2-70ac-5760-9ddc-ebf3b618c556" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afb02c14-0e39-54c3-8fb8-8b2b3a885193" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10245252-29bb-5324-a581-26085a39fe28" "answer-afb02c14-0e39-54c3-8fb8-8b2b3a885193" "answer-258a35a6-2b3a-5e86-8b1f-0ce644f7d05d" "answer-16a66103-9d90-5322-91a9-b6156d9743b5" "answer-fd6a0e9a-46c1-5683-94a3-cd1426ac3273"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10245252-29bb-5324-a581-26085a39fe28" :answer/id #uuid "10245252-29bb-5324-a581-26085a39fe28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$4.94$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afb02c14-0e39-54c3-8fb8-8b2b3a885193" :answer/id #uuid "afb02c14-0e39-54c3-8fb8-8b2b3a885193" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$5.34$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-258a35a6-2b3a-5e86-8b1f-0ce644f7d05d" :answer/id #uuid "258a35a6-2b3a-5e86-8b1f-0ce644f7d05d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$5.64$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16a66103-9d90-5322-91a9-b6156d9743b5" :answer/id #uuid "16a66103-9d90-5322-91a9-b6156d9743b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$5.84$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd6a0e9a-46c1-5683-94a3-cd1426ac3273" :answer/id #uuid "fd6a0e9a-46c1-5683-94a3-cd1426ac3273" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$5.94$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186495042 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fa60ae23-8081-566e-ab07-1797ceb80d43" "question-b32ba521-b62e-5f22-bb06-26d27c73470d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fa60ae23-8081-566e-ab07-1797ceb80d43" :question/id #uuid "fa60ae23-8081-566e-ab07-1797ceb80d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-68901" :question/problem "Lucy's Treats sells three different boxes of raisins: \n\n- Box $A$ contains $12$ ounces, and costs $$2.28\\,.$\n\n- Box $B$ contains $32$ ounces,  and costs $$5.44\\,.$\n\n- Box $C$ contains $22$ ounces, and costs $$3.52\\,.$\n\nWhich box of raisins is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the box with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the price by the total number of ounces.   \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n2.28÷12=0.19\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$0.19.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $B,$ we get\n\n$$\n5.44÷32=0.17\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $B$ is $$0.17.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of ounces in box $C,$ we get\n\n$$\n3.52÷22=0.16\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$0.16.$\n\nFrom the above, we see that box $C$ has the lowest unit price of $$0.16/\\text{oz}.$ Therefore, box $C$ offers the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-580ccd6e-f901-58f3-a184-32b32c159856"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-580ccd6e-f901-58f3-a184-32b32c159856" :answer-field/id #uuid "580ccd6e-f901-58f3-a184-32b32c159856" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-121f19df-f7ec-5869-a45c-be189aec34af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ec85867-3f96-5f17-bbbb-317d242f0548" "answer-1ca66867-a609-5af2-ba9f-24b54371b40b" "answer-194f3cf1-5137-5229-bdee-281142e918b9" "answer-ad5f5f79-d0dc-59fb-b9e3-e7f3e5825455" "answer-121f19df-f7ec-5869-a45c-be189aec34af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ec85867-3f96-5f17-bbbb-317d242f0548" :answer/id #uuid "9ec85867-3f96-5f17-bbbb-317d242f0548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ca66867-a609-5af2-ba9f-24b54371b40b" :answer/id #uuid "1ca66867-a609-5af2-ba9f-24b54371b40b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-194f3cf1-5137-5229-bdee-281142e918b9" :answer/id #uuid "194f3cf1-5137-5229-bdee-281142e918b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad5f5f79-d0dc-59fb-b9e3-e7f3e5825455" :answer/id #uuid "ad5f5f79-d0dc-59fb-b9e3-e7f3e5825455" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-121f19df-f7ec-5869-a45c-be189aec34af" :answer/id #uuid "121f19df-f7ec-5869-a45c-be189aec34af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186495043 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6ad6d7d2-b42a-533b-a893-138de3271ac7" "question-25c7031c-7a26-5c4d-b79f-0063afe0df6f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6ad6d7d2-b42a-533b-a893-138de3271ac7" :question/id #uuid "6ad6d7d2-b42a-533b-a893-138de3271ac7" :question/math-academy-id "q-68919" :question/problem "At Joe's market, the unit price of tomatoes is $$5$ per pound. How many pounds of tomatoes can Geena buy for $$1?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$5$ per pound (dollars per pound). To find how many pounds of tomatoes she can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in pounds per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n5\\,\\text{dollars per pound}\\,\\to \\,1÷5=0.2\\,\\text{pounds per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.2$ pounds per dollar. Therefore, Geena can buy $0.2$ pounds of tomatoes for $1$ dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4ee093f1-885a-5858-9c9e-fa0b646988c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4ee093f1-885a-5858-9c9e-fa0b646988c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee093f1-885a-5858-9c9e-fa0b646988c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f7498fbd-777b-58c7-84a1-2f148a7f13d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7498fbd-777b-58c7-84a1-2f148a7f13d7" "answer-df252277-1b3a-5f73-86c9-24b594684032" "answer-e1a47dec-e10b-5077-a7ac-7a5a62c0ed53" "answer-67a910b8-a9f6-545c-83d3-a9a8462d00f2" "answer-18257edf-9868-553b-81b1-2c63d81b6b3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7498fbd-777b-58c7-84a1-2f148a7f13d7" :answer/id #uuid "f7498fbd-777b-58c7-84a1-2f148a7f13d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.2$ pounds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df252277-1b3a-5f73-86c9-24b594684032" :answer/id #uuid "df252277-1b3a-5f73-86c9-24b594684032" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.25$ pounds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1a47dec-e10b-5077-a7ac-7a5a62c0ed53" :answer/id #uuid "e1a47dec-e10b-5077-a7ac-7a5a62c0ed53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.3$ pounds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67a910b8-a9f6-545c-83d3-a9a8462d00f2" :answer/id #uuid "67a910b8-a9f6-545c-83d3-a9a8462d00f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.4$ pounds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18257edf-9868-553b-81b1-2c63d81b6b3b" :answer/id #uuid "18257edf-9868-553b-81b1-2c63d81b6b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.5$ pounds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b32ba521-b62e-5f22-bb06-26d27c73470d" :question/id #uuid "b32ba521-b62e-5f22-bb06-26d27c73470d" :question/math-academy-id "q-91913" :question/problem "In a snack store, there are three different types of cookies that come in boxes: \n\n- Box $A$ contains $13$ pounds, and costs $$3.77\\,.$\n\n- Box $B$ contains $10.5$ pounds, and costs $$3.15\\,.$\n\n- Box $C$ contains $12$ pounds, and costs $$3.48\\,.$\n\nWhich box of cookies is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the cost by the total number of pounds.  \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in box $A$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.77÷13=0.29\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$0.29$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in box $B$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.15÷10.5=0.30\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of bag $B$ is $$0.30$  per pound.\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of pounds in box $C$,  we get\n\n$$\n3.48÷12=0.29\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$0.29$  per pound.\n\nFrom the above, we see that boxes $A$ and $C$ have the lowest unit price. Therefore, boxes $A$ and $C$ are the best deals." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41add624-7a03-5829-b64c-9f93149a5a5e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41add624-7a03-5829-b64c-9f93149a5a5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "41add624-7a03-5829-b64c-9f93149a5a5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-052a5fc9-a08a-5e7c-b988-4b6314c92427" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3220a4ae-203a-54bc-8dc9-0404a172e8e0" "answer-052a5fc9-a08a-5e7c-b988-4b6314c92427" "answer-e8f6004b-175f-5126-90f5-0f335d97919a" "answer-9da09a2e-4db0-5717-b2b6-a9683981734e" "answer-4ac7e5ef-63b7-5158-a86b-66afea0c52dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3220a4ae-203a-54bc-8dc9-0404a172e8e0" :answer/id #uuid "3220a4ae-203a-54bc-8dc9-0404a172e8e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-052a5fc9-a08a-5e7c-b988-4b6314c92427" :answer/id #uuid "052a5fc9-a08a-5e7c-b988-4b6314c92427" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8f6004b-175f-5126-90f5-0f335d97919a" :answer/id #uuid "e8f6004b-175f-5126-90f5-0f335d97919a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9da09a2e-4db0-5717-b2b6-a9683981734e" :answer/id #uuid "9da09a2e-4db0-5717-b2b6-a9683981734e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ac7e5ef-63b7-5158-a86b-66afea0c52dc" :answer/id #uuid "4ac7e5ef-63b7-5158-a86b-66afea0c52dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-25c7031c-7a26-5c4d-b79f-0063afe0df6f" :question/id #uuid "25c7031c-7a26-5c4d-b79f-0063afe0df6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-355712" :question/problem "At the deli, the unit price of specialty cheese is $$2$ per ounce. How many ounces of specialty cheese can Rohan buy for $$1?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$2$ per ounce (dollars per ounce). To find how many ounces of specialty cheese he can buy for  $$1,$ we need to find the unit rate in ounces per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n2\\,\\text{dollars per ounce}\\,\\to \\,1÷2=0.5\\,\\text{ounces per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $0.5$ ounces per dollar. Therefore, Rohan can buy $0.5$ ounces of specialty cheese for $1$ dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-11cd4261-4362-564b-a6e4-d1df079c1ba9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-11cd4261-4362-564b-a6e4-d1df079c1ba9" :answer-field/id #uuid "11cd4261-4362-564b-a6e4-d1df079c1ba9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4461a9e0-563a-5ac6-903f-d8ac88236689" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c9674547-8ff9-5492-8ca5-922e240e0938" "answer-90f24755-d4bb-5615-a831-d25c0b5723db" "answer-a9e7d584-2f09-5ba1-a845-e468f2ab21c2" "answer-55ca1c43-f050-5967-bd2b-52a28533f379" "answer-4461a9e0-563a-5ac6-903f-d8ac88236689"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9674547-8ff9-5492-8ca5-922e240e0938" :answer/id #uuid "c9674547-8ff9-5492-8ca5-922e240e0938" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.1$ ounces" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90f24755-d4bb-5615-a831-d25c0b5723db" :answer/id #uuid "90f24755-d4bb-5615-a831-d25c0b5723db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.2$ ounces" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9e7d584-2f09-5ba1-a845-e468f2ab21c2" :answer/id #uuid "a9e7d584-2f09-5ba1-a845-e468f2ab21c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.25$ ounces" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55ca1c43-f050-5967-bd2b-52a28533f379" :answer/id #uuid "55ca1c43-f050-5967-bd2b-52a28533f379" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.4$ ounces" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4461a9e0-563a-5ac6-903f-d8ac88236689" :answer/id #uuid "4461a9e0-563a-5ac6-903f-d8ac88236689" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0.5$ ounces" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-cb8ff5bb-d59c-5914-bb61-57ac943c0155" :activity/id #uuid "cb8ff5bb-d59c-5914-bb61-57ac943c0155" :activity/title "Working With Unit Prices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186495275 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-fcb274d6-4201-5c3e-bf1f-dac0c5b949ad" "step-b67b97a8-1d26-577a-b9f1-8e74866dde08" "step-75590325-0b56-5c97-a717-ef93b875f262" "step-6808d3f3-1bd6-54f5-b886-4da1e7511ffe" "step-a6853681-9bf8-57e0-aa5a-d730ef04cfc0"] :activity/first-step "step-fcb274d6-4201-5c3e-bf1f-dac0c5b949ad" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fcb274d6-4201-5c3e-bf1f-dac0c5b949ad" :step/id #uuid "fcb274d6-4201-5c3e-bf1f-dac0c5b949ad" :step/content "question-c993b31b-1739-52ac-a2f5-55deea55eaf7" :step/next "step-b67b97a8-1d26-577a-b9f1-8e74866dde08" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b67b97a8-1d26-577a-b9f1-8e74866dde08" :step/id #uuid "b67b97a8-1d26-577a-b9f1-8e74866dde08" :step/content "question-fa60ae23-8081-566e-ab07-1797ceb80d43" :step/next "step-75590325-0b56-5c97-a717-ef93b875f262" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-75590325-0b56-5c97-a717-ef93b875f262" :step/id #uuid "75590325-0b56-5c97-a717-ef93b875f262" :step/content "question-6ad6d7d2-b42a-533b-a893-138de3271ac7" :step/next "step-6808d3f3-1bd6-54f5-b886-4da1e7511ffe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6808d3f3-1bd6-54f5-b886-4da1e7511ffe" :step/id #uuid "6808d3f3-1bd6-54f5-b886-4da1e7511ffe" :step/content "question-b32ba521-b62e-5f22-bb06-26d27c73470d" :step/next "step-a6853681-9bf8-57e0-aa5a-d730ef04cfc0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a6853681-9bf8-57e0-aa5a-d730ef04cfc0" :step/id #uuid "a6853681-9bf8-57e0-aa5a-d730ef04cfc0" :step/content "question-25c7031c-7a26-5c4d-b79f-0063afe0df6f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054702 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6909c4f4-167d-501d-93f8-5aca9ebb11ed"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054512 :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}\\left[(2x-1)^3(x-2)^9\\right].$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply the product rule and the power rule to get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}\\left[(2x-1)^3(x-2)^9\\right]   &= \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(2x-1)^3\\cdot  \\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(x-2)^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    &= \\left(\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(2x-1)\\right)^3\\cdot  \\left(\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 3}(x-2)\\right)^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    &= (2\\cdot 3 -1)^3\\cdot (3-2)^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    &= 5^3 \\cdot 1^9\\[3pt]\n                                                                                    & = 125.\n}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054513 :question/problem "The figure below shows the graph of $f(x).$ Determine $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2} \\left(\\dfrac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2}\\right)^3.$\n\n![](images/50/5059a2cee34ad8547bf1af6239ab4a8356e715cd920707cf5f33d2de105a5c1d.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we find $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2} f(x)=3.$ Therefore, using the power rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}{(\\frac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2})}^{3} & ={({lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{2-7x}{xf(x)+2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2-7(2)}{(2\\cdot 3)+2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-12}{8})}^{3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{-3}{2})}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{27}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054604 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-156d5c20-d8d9-52c6-bf0a-a41e2c4bb6cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054518 :question/problem "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 1} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+8}}{x-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+8}}{x-2}\n=\\dfrac{\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1} \\sqrt{x+8}}{\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\nApplying the root rule in the numerator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\sqrt{x+8} & =\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to 1}(x+8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the denominator, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}(x-2) & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+8}}{x-2} & =\\frac{3}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054605 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-522ad648-b326-5d90-9d3d-5351c0a03cfc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054519 :question/worked-solution "According to the power rule and the quotient rules,\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}{(\\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}-1})}^{2/3} & ={(\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)}{{lim}_{x\\to -2}({x}^{2}-1)})}^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find from the graph that the limit of the numerator is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow -2} f(x)=1.\n$$\n\n We also calculate the limit of the denominator as\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}({x}^{2}-1) & =(-2)^{2}-1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n So we get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}{(\\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}-1})}^{2/3} & ={(\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)}{{lim}_{x\\to -2}({x}^{2}-1)})}^{2/3} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2/3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233993 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f764e06-5d80-555d-8746-1b05ecbf0c86"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f764e06-5d80-555d-8746-1b05ecbf0c86" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f764e06-5d80-555d-8746-1b05ecbf0c86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c0df1c26-3aa5-5e3c-8200-ef9d0a2e3adc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05ded502-a64c-59eb-b7d3-1edbc975c8ad" "answer-81325284-9641-5f8d-97f8-687ea6659699" "answer-3ceb6ed1-d121-5435-888c-425931472192" "answer-8242f5d4-885b-5673-94ee-6897001038fe" "answer-c0df1c26-3aa5-5e3c-8200-ef9d0a2e3adc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05ded502-a64c-59eb-b7d3-1edbc975c8ad" :answer/id #uuid "05ded502-a64c-59eb-b7d3-1edbc97