b/id "answer-91a02bc0-8a2d-5270-a0b4-b9c6395fc706" :answer/id #uuid "91a02bc0-8a2d-5270-a0b4-b9c6395fc706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[7]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5ba0bae-ecb1-5788-9a40-c0d5b364deaf" :answer/id #uuid "a5ba0bae-ecb1-5788-9a40-c0d5b364deaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{ DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-156d5c20-d8d9-52c6-bf0a-a41e2c4bb6cd" :question/id #uuid "156d5c20-d8d9-52c6-bf0a-a41e2c4bb6cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-77741" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3}=\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\sqrt[3]{10x-3})}{{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-3)}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\nApplying the root rule in the numerator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}(\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}) & =\\sqrt[3]{10(3)-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{30-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{27} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the denominator, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}({x}^{2}-3) & =(3)^{2}-3 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{10x-3}}{{x}^{2}-3} & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32c46171-eabc-556f-8329-ffe46779d9b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32c46171-eabc-556f-8329-ffe46779d9b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "32c46171-eabc-556f-8329-ffe46779d9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36b3766c-1ae9-5be4-b0ba-9fd174da5698" :answer-field/choices ["answer-094bbce6-b3ec-5cc2-b5d6-74f6b386c8ee" "answer-b89c254c-c17d-5295-bc07-c24266eb0f55" "answer-36b3766c-1ae9-5be4-b0ba-9fd174da5698" "answer-495b98a8-0a0e-599c-827d-bc7c6e909cf2" "answer-5da93ba3-774d-5fb6-911a-3522020430fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-094bbce6-b3ec-5cc2-b5d6-74f6b386c8ee" :answer/id #uuid "094bbce6-b3ec-5cc2-b5d6-74f6b386c8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b89c254c-c17d-5295-bc07-c24266eb0f55" :answer/id #uuid "b89c254c-c17d-5295-bc07-c24266eb0f55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36b3766c-1ae9-5be4-b0ba-9fd174da5698" :answer/id #uuid "36b3766c-1ae9-5be4-b0ba-9fd174da5698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-495b98a8-0a0e-599c-827d-bc7c6e909cf2" :answer/id #uuid "495b98a8-0a0e-599c-827d-bc7c6e909cf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5da93ba3-774d-5fb6-911a-3522020430fe" :answer/id #uuid "5da93ba3-774d-5fb6-911a-3522020430fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-522ad648-b326-5d90-9d3d-5351c0a03cfc" :question/id #uuid "522ad648-b326-5d90-9d3d-5351c0a03cfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-100306" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b12ba04b803d58c6cacf4fc781db5c7032c3aedad80506c101bf084109ebd797.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to -2}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4(f(x))^{3}-3{x}^{2}}{2}}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=-1.$\n\nApplying the root rule, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4(f(x))^{3}-3{x}^{2}}{2}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{lim}_{x\\to -2}(\\frac{4(f(x))^{3}-3{x}^{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4\\cdot (-1)^{3}-3(-2)^{2}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{-4-12}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{-8} \\\\  & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-81cfc4b2-47d0-50ed-a06c-623ea25dae23"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-81cfc4b2-47d0-50ed-a06c-623ea25dae23" :answer-field/id #uuid "81cfc4b2-47d0-50ed-a06c-623ea25dae23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-602172b3-6445-5c63-91e9-d860394ce5a1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-602172b3-6445-5c63-91e9-d860394ce5a1" "answer-79827563-1b5d-5c99-902a-4ea904d05b4d" "answer-f672a463-52c0-5b34-9a86-4f4728479311" "answer-b8839d8b-e0bd-5cb4-8bde-c168499e0d23" "answer-71a5e4f2-139f-523f-9c38-312f34b1bd6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-602172b3-6445-5c63-91e9-d860394ce5a1" :answer/id #uuid "602172b3-6445-5c63-91e9-d860394ce5a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79827563-1b5d-5c99-902a-4ea904d05b4d" :answer/id #uuid "79827563-1b5d-5c99-902a-4ea904d05b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f672a463-52c0-5b34-9a86-4f4728479311" :answer/id #uuid "f672a463-52c0-5b34-9a86-4f4728479311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8839d8b-e0bd-5cb4-8bde-c168499e0d23" :answer/id #uuid "b8839d8b-e0bd-5cb4-8bde-c168499e0d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71a5e4f2-139f-523f-9c38-312f34b1bd6b" :answer/id #uuid "71a5e4f2-139f-523f-9c38-312f34b1bd6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055954 :tutorial/content "The **power rule** states that the limit of a power is the power of the limit. More precisely, if $n$ is any positive integer and $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow a}f(x)=L,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to a}(f(x))^{n}={({lim}_{x\\to a}f(x))}^{n}={L}^{n}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, with the power rule, we can evaluate a limit like \n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2}(3x-4)^{8}\n$$\n\n by evaluating the limit of the expression within parentheses and then taking the power of the result.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}(3x-4)^{8} & ={({lim}_{x\\to 2}(3x-4))}^{8} \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 2-4)^{8} \\\\  & ={2}^{8} \\\\  & =256\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055955 :tutorial/content "The **root rule** states that the limit of a root is the root of the limit (provided that the root exists).\n\nMore precisely, if $n$ is any positive integer and $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow a}f(x)=L,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to a}\\sqrt[n]{f(x)}=\\sqrt[n]{{lim}_{x\\to a}f(x)}=\\sqrt[n]{L}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, with the root rule, we can evaluate a limit like \n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 2}\\sqrt{3x-2}\n$$\n\n by evaluating the limit of the expression within the root and then taking the root of the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt{3x-2} & =\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to 2}(3x-2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot 2-2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055956 :tutorial/content "If we combine the power rule and the root rule, then we get the following useful generalization: if $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow a}f(x)=L,$ then for any fraction $p/q,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow a}\\left(f(x)\\right)^{p/q} =  \\left(\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow a} f(x)\\right)^{p/q} = L^{p/q}\n$$\n\nprovided that $L^{p/q}$ exists.\n\nFor example, we can evaluate a limit like \n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{y\\rightarrow 64} y^{-1/6}\n$$\n\n by evaluating the limit of $y$ and then exponentiating the result to the fractional exponent:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 64}{y}^{-1/6} & ={({lim}_{y\\to 64}y)}^{-1/6} \\\\  & =(64)^{-1/6} \\\\  & ={({2}^{6})}^{-1/6} \\\\  & ={2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054899 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186051350 :answer-field/choices 17592186051351] [:db/retract 17592186051350 :answer-field/choices 17592186051352] [:db/retract 17592186051362 :answer-field/choices 17592186051363] [:db/retract 17592186051362 :answer-field/choices 17592186051364] [:db/retract 17592186051362 :answer-field/choices 17592186051365] [:db/retract 17592186051362 :answer-field/choices 17592186051366] [:db/retract 17592186051362 :answer-field/choices 17592186051367] {:db/id 17592186054848 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bf7a3bf9-7841-5c39-8953-649f06640b22"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054425 :question/problem "List the elements of the following set: \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{a, c,3, \\{c,3 \\}, \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}\\big\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the set $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\na, \\quad c, \\quad 3, \\quad \\{c,3\\}, \\quad \\emptyset, \\quad \\{\\emptyset\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!**\n\n- The elements $c,3,$ and $\\{c,3\\}$ are three separate entities. The first two are the elements $c$ and $3,$ and the third is a set *containing* these two elements.\n\n- The elements $\\emptyset$ and $\\{ \\emptyset \\}$ are also separate entities. The first one is the empty set (i.e., the set containing no elements), while the second is a set that contains the empty set." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054849 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-68a9ef69-1a68-5a42-bd02-0ed93671db30" "question-f2f32264-6492-5e60-8c09-298d7626357d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054426 :question/problem "Which of the following is **not** a set?\n\nI. $\\{ 2, 4, 6 \\}$\n\nII. $\\{ \\{ 2 \\}, \\{ 4, 6 \\} \\}$\n\nIII. $2, 4, 6$\n\nIV. $\\emptyset$" :question/worked-solution "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $\\emptyset.$\n\n- $\\{ 2, 4, 6 \\}$ is a set. The elements are $2,$ $4,$ and $6,$ and they are listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\{ \\{ 2 \\}, \\{ 4, 6 \\} \\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\{ 2 \\}$ and $\\{ 4, 6 \\},$ and are listed between the two outermost braces.\n\n- $2, 4, 6$ is *not* a set. The numbers $2,$ $4,$ and $6$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\emptyset$ is the empty set. Therefore, it is a set.\n\nIn conclusion, only III is not a set." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6ae10c4a-b478-5b9e-9599-7eb7b75dca9d" "question-6b96bbb9-30d0-511e-a26c-5b394ffc1b3c" "question-f10fdf14-c3b0-5ff7-a1e1-67a02a7a3852"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054427 :question/problem "Write the following statement using element notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $1$ and $2$ are elements of a set $S,$ but $3,$ $4,$ and $5$ are not." :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a \\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a \\notin S.$\n\n- Since $1$ and $2$ are elements of $S,$ we write $1,2 \\in S.$\n\n- Since $3,$ $4,$ and $5$ are *not* elements of $S,$ we write $3,4,5 \\notin S.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$$\n1,2 \\in S\\quad \\textrm{and}\\quad 3,4,5 \\notin S\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054851 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-101cf0dd-9e7d-5358-b3ec-977545014b49" "question-76066cd5-d606-50ce-8894-909f30c9f6a3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054428 :question/problem "Express the following sets using an ellipsis:\n\n- The set $X$ of all positive integers greater than or equal to $10$\n\n- The set $Y$ of integers less than zero\n\n- The set $A$ of all natural numbers greater than $5$ and less than $5\\, 005$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an ellipsis means \"and so on up to\" if it's followed by a specific element, or \"and so on\" if not.\n\n- To express the set $X,$ we start with the first positive integer greater than or equal to $10,$ which is $10.$ The next integer is $11,$ the one after that is $12,$ and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n\n$$\nX = \\{10, 11, 12, \\ldots \\}\n$$\n\n- To express the set $Y,$ we start with the first integer less than zero, which is $-1.$ The next integer less than zero is $-2,$ the one after that is $-3,$ and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n\n$$\nY = \\{ -1, -2, -3, \\ldots \\}\n$$\n\nHowever, note that it is conventional to write a set of numbers from least to greatest, just like is shown on the number line. Writing the elements of $Y$ from least to greatest, we have\n\n$$\nY = \\{ \\ldots , -3, -2, -1\\}.\n$$\n\n- To express the set $A,$ we start with the first positive integer greater than $5,$ which is $6.$ The next integer is $7,$ the one after that is $8,$ and so on up to $5\\, 004$ (the largest integer less than $5\\, 005$). So, we have\n\n$$\nA = \\{6, 7, 8, \\ldots , 5004\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054970 :question/problem "Which of the following is an element of the set $C=\\{\\{a\\},\\,b,\\,\\{c\\},\\,d,\\,\\{e\\}\\}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of our set are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{a\\},\\,b,\\,\\{c\\},\\,d,\\,\\{e\\}\n$$\n\nAmong the given options, the only element that belongs to the set is $\\{e\\}.$\n\n**Watch out!** Note that $e$ is *not* an element of our set. Our set contains an element $\\{e\\}$ that is a set itself." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051350 :answer-field/correct "answer-5e87d1b9-c21c-5e07-8bcb-e7801cafe650" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dbed2e9b-2062-58e1-bbcb-34bffd5958e8" "answer-5e87d1b9-c21c-5e07-8bcb-e7801cafe650"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbed2e9b-2062-58e1-bbcb-34bffd5958e8" :answer/id #uuid "dbed2e9b-2062-58e1-bbcb-34bffd5958e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{d\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e87d1b9-c21c-5e07-8bcb-e7801cafe650" :answer/id #uuid "5e87d1b9-c21c-5e07-8bcb-e7801cafe650" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{e\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf7a3bf9-7841-5c39-8953-649f06640b22" :question/id #uuid "bf7a3bf9-7841-5c39-8953-649f06640b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-181262" :question/problem "Which of the following is an element of the set $A=\\{♢,\\,10,\\,a,\\,◻\\}?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of our set are as follows:\n\n$$\n♢,\\,10,\\,a,\\,◻\n$$\n\nAmong the given options, the only element that belongs to the set is $◻.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c41e6d8-d02a-5d03-aa80-6b777df73834"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c41e6d8-d02a-5d03-aa80-6b777df73834" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c41e6d8-d02a-5d03-aa80-6b777df73834" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-24a04d7d-0766-53f9-bf1a-56af16878e80" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6e44578a-0359-5902-888e-df2fb5a3bd0e" "answer-84feaf94-72bf-5421-abe7-2cb440d49da6" "answer-8e5dea63-94f7-5b8d-8a9d-2375d5e03ec5" "answer-aed08239-7725-54b6-a37b-ad604cc72dec" "answer-24a04d7d-0766-53f9-bf1a-56af16878e80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e44578a-0359-5902-888e-df2fb5a3bd0e" :answer/id #uuid "6e44578a-0359-5902-888e-df2fb5a3bd0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84feaf94-72bf-5421-abe7-2cb440d49da6" :answer/id #uuid "84feaf94-72bf-5421-abe7-2cb440d49da6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e5dea63-94f7-5b8d-8a9d-2375d5e03ec5" :answer/id #uuid "8e5dea63-94f7-5b8d-8a9d-2375d5e03ec5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aed08239-7725-54b6-a37b-ad604cc72dec" :answer/id #uuid "aed08239-7725-54b6-a37b-ad604cc72dec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24a04d7d-0766-53f9-bf1a-56af16878e80" :answer/id #uuid "24a04d7d-0766-53f9-bf1a-56af16878e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "◻" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-68a9ef69-1a68-5a42-bd02-0ed93671db30" :question/id #uuid "68a9ef69-1a68-5a42-bd02-0ed93671db30" :question/math-academy-id "q-104392" :question/problem "Which of the following is **not** a set?" :question/worked-solution "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $∅.$\n\n- $\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}$ is *not* a set. The numbers $\\frac{2}{7},$ $\\frac{2}{5},$ $\\frac{2}{3},$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n\nAll the other choices are sets.\n\n- $\\{\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}\\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{2}{3},\\frac{1}{2}$ and they are listed between two braces.\n\n- $\\{\\{\\}\\}$ is a set. It contains a single element, $\\{\\},$ and this element is between two braces.\n\n- $\\{\\}$ is a set. It is the null set.\n\n- $∅$ is a set. It is the null set." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4989f7b-3998-56d8-84b3-b2b2b96bef9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4989f7b-3998-56d8-84b3-b2b2b96bef9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4989f7b-3998-56d8-84b3-b2b2b96bef9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-847ea62c-8079-5329-b9a6-20b01100c875" :answer-field/choices ["answer-847ea62c-8079-5329-b9a6-20b01100c875" "answer-a6ae7272-dfb4-51e4-813a-3b640ded878e" "answer-6e636f0b-5913-5738-8061-83223afb839d" "answer-3b6319c4-4efb-5c74-bead-1ca09a8e128b" "answer-650db520-6fe2-5a0f-a847-f67969871c86"] :db/en