ked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{t}) & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{t}}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{t}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{t}}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{t})^{-1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}+(\\sqrt{t})^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\sqrt{t}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{t+1}{\\sqrt{t}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{t+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ad40e26-871d-5735-a53a-4f67d90f045a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ad40e26-871d-5735-a53a-4f67d90f045a" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ad40e26-871d-5735-a53a-4f67d90f045a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95c44a7e-df43-50bc-a5cd-70761f467a3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e707ecd-c178-55dc-854b-4e79cc7e337f" "answer-95c44a7e-df43-50bc-a5cd-70761f467a3e" "answer-ea931382-e509-5b41-b3c4-5c291f5e42e9" "answer-ebb5e7fd-8833-595e-8978-65b4198dc5b8" "answer-fc20631b-64e7-56b3-b072-c5a52e914f14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e707ecd-c178-55dc-854b-4e79cc7e337f" :answer/id #uuid "5e707ecd-c178-55dc-854b-4e79cc7e337f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95c44a7e-df43-50bc-a5cd-70761f467a3e" :answer/id #uuid "95c44a7e-df43-50bc-a5cd-70761f467a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{t+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea931382-e509-5b41-b3c4-5c291f5e42e9" :answer/id #uuid "ea931382-e509-5b41-b3c4-5c291f5e42e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{t}}{t+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebb5e7fd-8833-595e-8978-65b4198dc5b8" :answer/id #uuid "ebb5e7fd-8833-595e-8978-65b4198dc5b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc20631b-64e7-56b3-b072-c5a52e914f14" :answer/id #uuid "fc20631b-64e7-56b3-b072-c5a52e914f14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{t+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa7fb149-1626-56db-aafd-3693bf4f703f" :question/id #uuid "aa7fb149-1626-56db-aafd-3693bf4f703f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340820" :question/problem "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{sech}⁡1.$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{sech}⁡1=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡1 & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{1}+{e}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(e+\\frac{1}{e})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{e})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{{e}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-414b1934-a60c-5b00-b690-7baace00611d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-414b1934-a60c-5b00-b690-7baace00611d" :answer-field/id #uuid "414b1934-a60c-5b00-b690-7baace00611d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-972c2fc3-94db-5577-8544-208982267693" :answer-field/choices ["answer-972c2fc3-94db-5577-8544-208982267693"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-972c2fc3-94db-5577-8544-208982267693" :answer/id #uuid "972c2fc3-94db-5577-8544-208982267693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{{e}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-558ac263-8cd5-56f3-9f79-c76511bfad24" :question/id #uuid "558ac263-8cd5-56f3-9f79-c76511bfad24" :question/math-academy-id "q-125700" :question/problem "$$\n\nGiven that $z>0,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)?$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z) & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{z}^{-1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{z+(z)^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(z+\\frac{1}{z})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{{z}^{2}+1}{z})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2z}{{z}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5fdec476-5453-533f-ba1c-e55425c49aeb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5fdec476-5453-533f-ba1c-e55425c49aeb" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fdec476-5453-533f-ba1c-e55425c49aeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-30f00be7-84e1-5894-80e6-57a208b88c62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-041ce06a-3f86-5e30-a3fa-868512983162" "answer-30f00be7-84e1-5894-80e6-57a208b88c62" "answer-69fcfaa8-1f10-5a22-a6a0-edbaf0ccf489" "answer-d881232c-3fdd-51aa-bc26-114e5f59ead6" "answer-cf67f338-3bbd-5b2b-b73c-d6f9874a475c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-041ce06a-3f86-5e30-a3fa-868512983162" :answer/id #uuid "041ce06a-3f86-5e30-a3fa-868512983162" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2z}{1-{z}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30f00be7-84e1-5894-80e6-57a208b88c62" :answer/id #uuid "30f00be7-84e1-5894-80e6-57a208b88c62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2z}{{z}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69fcfaa8-1f10-5a22-a6a0-edbaf0ccf489" :answer/id #uuid "69fcfaa8-1f10-5a22-a6a0-edbaf0ccf489" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2z}{{z}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d881232c-3fdd-51aa-bc26-114e5f59ead6" :answer/id #uuid "d881232c-3fdd-51aa-bc26-114e5f59ead6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{z}{{z}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf67f338-3bbd-5b2b-b73c-d6f9874a475c" :answer/id #uuid "cf67f338-3bbd-5b2b-b73c-d6f9874a475c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{z}{{z}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a717dc62-f0d0-579e-9ded-2923a5f96442" :question/id #uuid "a717dc62-f0d0-579e-9ded-2923a5f96442" :question/math-academy-id "q-300677" :question/problem "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{5}}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{5})^{-1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}+(\\sqrt{5})^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\sqrt{5}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5fea91a9-b09a-5a02-bb27-07b1b9e3e60e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5fea91a9-b09a-5a02-bb27-07b1b9e3e60e" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fea91a9-b09a-5a02-bb27-07b1b9e3e60e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e3d08d87-5e72-5cee-a7d3-5556366a9ad0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3d08d87-5e72-5cee-a7d3-5556366a9ad0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3d08d87-5e72-5cee-a7d3-5556366a9ad0" :answer/id #uuid "e3d08d87-5e72-5cee-a7d3-5556366a9ad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-221afffc-6058-53ae-8f4b-ca54ee801c93" :question/id #uuid "221afffc-6058-53ae-8f4b-ca54ee801c93" :question/math-academy-id "q-300672" :question/problem "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{sech}⁡7.$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{sech}⁡7=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sech}⁡7 & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{7}+{e}^{-7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b0c89911-0451-57b8-bb87-aa95e175c6d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0c89911-0451-57b8-bb87-aa95e175c6d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c89911-0451-57b8-bb87-aa95e175c6d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7fb09ddc-f58b-57c4-b0f8-adf015a93e1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fb09ddc-f58b-57c4-b0f8-adf015a93e1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fb09ddc-f58b-57c4-b0f8-adf015a93e1d" :answer/id #uuid "7fb09ddc-f58b-57c4-b0f8-adf015a93e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{e^{7}+e^{-7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f714102a-964b-532c-b041-8149ac6f2160" :question/id #uuid "f714102a-964b-532c-b041-8149ac6f2160" :question/math-academy-id "q-340828" :question/problem "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{coth}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{coth}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2})=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fourth definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2})}}{1-{e}^{-2(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}}}{1-{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}}{1-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1+\\frac{1}{4})}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}÷\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cad4afc6-9656-5283-837f-a8416585d0c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cad4afc6-9656-5283-837f-a8416585d0c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cad4afc6-9656-5283-837f-a8416585d0c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ffcd5731-2069-5efb-ac00-2f8ff3414dd5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ffcd5731-2069-5efb-ac00-2f8ff3414dd5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffcd5731-2069-5efb-ac00-2f8ff3414dd5" :answer/id #uuid "ffcd5731-2069-5efb-ac00-2f8ff3414dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8d94db5-30b8-5d58-91bd-e8bbc8dd17c5" :question/id #uuid "a8d94db5-30b8-5d58-91bd-e8bbc8dd17c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-300702" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\operatorname{coth}⁡3.$ **Do not round** your answer.\n$$$$\n\n$\\operatorname{coth}⁡3=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡3 & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3)}+1}{{e}^{2(3)}-1}=\\frac{{e}^{6}+1}{{e}^{6}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c2ce44e-4f1e-519d-a1b9-c6fbfc2dc7c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c2ce44e-4f1e-519d-a1b9-c6fbfc2dc7c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2ce44e-4f1e-519d-a1b9-c6fbfc2dc7c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fa02a9fd-da12-51d0-8e53-1443370bbe7a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa02a9fd-da12-51d0-8e53-1443370bbe7a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa02a9fd-da12-51d0-8e53-1443370bbe7a" :answer/id #uuid "fa02a9fd-da12-51d0-8e53-1443370bbe7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{6}+1}{e^{6}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167431 :question/problem "$$\n$\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}}+1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+1}{4-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165794 :answer-field/correct 17592186165798 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-9460a409-51fa-5175-bdf4-3dbd6c50a02e" :question/id #uuid "9460a409-51fa-5175-bdf4-3dbd6c50a02e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96551" :question/problem "$$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to  $\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w)?$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w) & =\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{w}^{2}}+1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{w}^{2}}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{w}^{2}+1}{4{w}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-757863fe-7e0e-5689-8cb2-227d3255cde1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-757863fe-7e0e-5689-8cb2-227d3255cde1" :answer-field/id #uuid "757863fe-7e0e-5689-8cb2-227d3255cde1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9034ce28-781f-5290-a4bd-28ca70b5eaef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a960892-473d-5c82-96ca-897b1bb8f323" "answer-fd4c3ed9-c949-547b-9857-3b5b4ceae3bf" "answer-a4d34bd2-ecc4-5d35-809a-9e7699733f9c" "answer-9034ce28-781f-5290-a4bd-28ca70b5eaef" "answer-f386b932-7e8f-5621-8229-0b3482f235be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a960892-473d-5c82-96ca-897b1bb8f323" :answer/id #uuid "2a960892-473d-5c82-96ca-897b1bb8f323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{w}^{2}+1}{2{w}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd4c3ed9-c949-547b-9857-3b5b4ceae3bf" :answer/id #uuid "fd4c3ed9-c949-547b-9857-3b5b4ceae3bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{w}^{2}-1}{2{w}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4d34bd2-ecc4-5d35-809a-9e7699733f9c" :answer/id #uuid "a4d34bd2-ecc4-5d35-809a-9e7699733f9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4w+1}{4w-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9034ce28-781f-5290-a4bd-28ca70b5eaef" :answer/id #uuid "9034ce28-781f-5290-a4bd-28ca70b5eaef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{w}^{2}+1}{4{w}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f386b932-7e8f-5621-8229-0b3482f235be" :answer/id #uuid "f386b932-7e8f-5621-8229-0b3482f235be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{w}^{2}-1}{4{w}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3203ea85-5b81-5f7d-8926-d8feaf4a8223" :question/id #uuid "3203ea85-5b81-5f7d-8926-d8feaf4a8223" :question/math-academy-id "q-340827" :question/problem "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\sqrt{5}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\sqrt{5})=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\sqrt{5})=\\frac{{e}^{2\\sqrt{5}}+1}{{e}^{2\\sqrt{5}}-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54daf4bc-b2ca-5b98-8707-23b1d3105f92"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54daf4bc-b2ca-5b98-8707-23b1d3105f92" :answer-field/id #uuid "54daf4bc-b2ca-5b98-8707-23b1d3105f92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c82cb5ba-2e25-559f-9acb-9f9f141709ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c82cb5ba-2e25-559f-9acb-9f9f141709ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c82cb5ba-2e25-559f-9acb-9f9f141709ec" :answer/id #uuid "c82cb5ba-2e25-559f-9acb-9f9f141709ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2\\sqrt{5}}+1}{e^{2\\sqrt{5}}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186158828 :answer-field/choices 17592186158832] [:db/retract 17592186158828 :answer-field/choices 17592186158833] [:db/retract 17592186158828 :answer-field/choices 17592186158829] [:db/retract 17592186158828 :answer-field/choices 17592186158831] {:db/id 17592186162059 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c53663ac-ef5b-58bc-a1be-8cea3868fa2f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162271 :question/problem "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables such that $X∼N(5,10)$ and $Y∼N(6,11).$ Find the distribution of the random variable $W=2X-5Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2})$, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W=2X-5Y & ∼N(2\\cdot 5+(-5)\\cdot 6,{2}^{2}\\cdot 10+(-5)^{2}\\cdot 11) \\\\  & ∼N(-20,315).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, $W∼N(-20,315).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158828 :answer-field/correct "answer-b488c945-d6ec-5534-9219-1a79a5b81aab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b488c945-d6ec-5534-9219-1a79a5b81aab" "answer-d878f46f-c745-5568-b119-bf0d3db97f4a" "answer-31e46495-af3d-5634-a059-e1014e45dee4" "answer-d9180bb9-7dcb-558b-87f6-8eb5ecb22a62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b488c945-d6ec-5534-9219-1a79a5b81aab" :answer/id #uuid "b488c945-d6ec-5534-9219-1a79a5b81aab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(-20,315)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d878f46f-c745-5568-b119-bf0d3db97f4a" :answer/id #uuid "d878f46f-c745-5568-b119-bf0d3db97f4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(-20,75)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e46495-af3d-5634-a059-e1014e45dee4" :answer/id #uuid "31e46495-af3d-5634-a059-e1014e45dee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(40,315)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9180bb9-7dcb-558b-87f6-8eb5ecb22a62" :answer/id #uuid "d9180bb9-7dcb-558b-87f6-8eb5ecb22a62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(40,75)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162060 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-65fa3d9f-f374-57d7-bfef-bf8f42da2e6e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-65fa3d9f-f374-57d7-bfef-bf8f42da2e6e" :question/id #uuid "65fa3d9f-f374-57d7-bfef-bf8f42da2e6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-109732" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1}∼N(5,3)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(8,4)$ are independent and $Y=4{X}_{1}-2{X}_{2},$ calculate $P(Y<14).$ Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ | $\\,0.8770\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ | $\\,0.8830\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ | $\\,0.8962\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.9115\\,$ | $\\,0.9131\\,$ | $\\,0.9147\\,$ | $\\,0.9162\\,$ | $\\,0.9177\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, the distribution of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y=4{X}_{1}-2{X}_{2} & ∼N(4{\\mu }_{1}-2{\\mu }_{2},16{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+4{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(20-16,48+16) \\\\  & ∼N(4,64).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =4$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{64}=8.$ \n\nWe want to find $P(Y<14).$ Thus, we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<14) & =P(Z<\\frac{14-4}{8}) \\\\  & =P(Z<1.25) \\\\  & =Φ(1.25)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(1.25)≈0.8944.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Y<14)≈0.89.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-63dec131-ea37-5a89-8bfa-e5223fe88c95"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-63dec131-ea37-5a89-8bfa-e5223fe88c95" :answer-field/id #uuid "63dec131-ea37-5a89-8bfa-e5223fe88c95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-67813379-2e23-5017-8ad9-a1a5d968c331" :answer-field/choices ["answer-82b05498-2c78-5f43-a343-c6dea0a978f0" "answer-67813379-2e23-5017-8ad9-a1a5d968c331" "answer-d2c794a4-ad11-517b-b863-482edd911ccf" "answer-f908b992-6ecb-5dd9-87da-ddd849714903" "answer-3f2a22da-8ee7-5c03-9406-a381bafad62e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82b05498-2c78-5f43-a343-c6dea0a978f0" :answer/id #uuid "82b05498-2c78-5f43-a343-c6dea0a978f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.87" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67813379-2e23-5017-8ad9-a1a5d968c331" :answer/id #uuid "67813379-2e23-5017-8ad9-a1a5d968c331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.89" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2c794a4-ad11-517b-b863-482edd911ccf" :answer/id #uuid "d2c794a4-ad11-517b-b863-482edd911ccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f908b992-6ecb-5dd9-87da-ddd849714903" :answer/id #uuid "f908b992-6ecb-5dd9-87da-ddd849714903" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f2a22da-8ee7-5c03-9406-a381bafad62e" :answer/id #uuid "3f2a22da-8ee7-5c03-9406-a381bafad62e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162061 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9dd9198d-6665-5e5e-bf17-48bb8a7b15be" "question-666db65e-d2dd-5df6-aa61-3e935a25f26e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9dd9198d-6665-5e5e-bf17-48bb8a7b15be" :question/id #uuid "9dd9198d-6665-5e5e-bf17-48bb8a7b15be" :question/math-academy-id "q-109748" :question/problem "The weights of some chocolate cookies are normally distributed with a mean of $10\\,\\text{g}$ and a variance of $1\\,{\\text{g}}^{2}.$ The weights of some oatcakes are normally distributed with a mean of $15\\,\\text{g}$ and a variance of $2\\,{\\text{g}}^{2}.$  If one chocolate cookie and one oatcake are randomly selected, what is the probability that $6$ times the weight of the cookie plus $4$ times the weight of oatcake is less than $120\\,\\text{g}$, but more than $100\\,\\text{g}?$ You may assume that the weights of the cookies and oatcakes are independent. \n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.5\\,$ | $\\,0.0062\\,$ | $\\,0.0060\\,$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ | $\\,0.0057\\,$ | $\\,0.0055\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0082\\,$ | $\\,0.0080\\,$ | $\\,0.0078\\,$ | $\\,0.0075\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0107\\,$ | $\\,0.0104\\,$ | $\\,0.0102\\,$ | $\\,0.0099\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ denote the weight of a chocolate cookie, and let $Y$ denote the weight of an oatcake. We want to find \n\n$$\nP(100<6X+4Y<120).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are  independent random variables such that $X∼N(10,1)$ and $Y∼N(15,2),$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6X+4Y & ∼N(6\\cdot 10+4\\cdot 15,36\\cdot 1+16\\cdot 2) \\\\  & ∼N(120,68).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variable $6X+4Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =120$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{68}.$\n\nTo find $P(100<6X+4Y<120),$ we convert $6X+4Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(100<6X+4Y<120) & =P(\\frac{100-120}{\\sqrt{68}}<Z<\\frac{120-120}{\\sqrt{68}}) \\\\  & ≈P(-2.43<Z<0) \\\\  & =P(Z<0)-P(Z\\le -2.43) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0)-P(Z\\le -2.43) \\\\  & =Φ(0)-Φ(-2.43)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.43) & ≈0.0075,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0) & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(100<6X+4Y<120) & ≈Φ(0)-Φ(-2.43) \\\\  & =0.5-0.0075 \\\\  & ≈0.4925.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f73640d-d4b8-5379-a9d2-f83257d2b179"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f73640d-d4b8-5379-a9d2-f83257d2b179" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f73640d-d4b8-5379-a9d2-f83257d2b179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c7b928a-dbf0-5c53-8e9c-221cc73604b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-953e7d4e-e884-5c5e-bebe-5d6c15fc8f60" "answer-1b7ed843-f01b-5ff0-9400-1f575ae46bc7" "answer-3c7b928a-dbf0-5c53-8e9c-221cc73604b6" "answer-c072162b-92cd-5039-9d7e-cf458cf7fc3b" "answer-a7650dd9-8eb4-5963-be58-a9d76c3de7ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-953e7d4e-e884-5c5e-bebe-5d6c15fc8f60" :answer/id #uuid "953e7d4e-e884-5c5e-bebe-5d6c15fc8f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4639" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b7ed843-f01b-5ff0-9400-1f575ae46bc7" :answer/id #uuid "1b7ed843-f01b-5ff0-9400-1f575ae46bc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4817" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c7b928a-dbf0-5c53-8e9c-221cc73604b6" :answer/id #uuid "3c7b928a-dbf0-5c53-8e9c-221cc73604b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4925" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c072162b-92cd-5039-9d7e-cf458cf7fc3b" :answer/id #uuid "c072162b-92cd-5039-9d7e-cf458cf7fc3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5003" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7650dd9-8eb4-5963-be58-a9d76c3de7ba" :answer/id #uuid "a7650dd9-8eb4-5963-be58-a9d76c3de7ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5153" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-666db65e-d2dd-5df6-aa61-3e935a25f26e" :question/id #uuid "666db65e-d2dd-5df6-aa61-3e935a25f26e" :question/math-academy-id "q-109755" :question/problem "A factory produces shovels, each consisting of a handle and a blade.\nThe length of a handle is normally distributed with a mean of $120$ centimeters and a variance of $0.14,$  while the length of a blade is normally distributed with a mean of $30$ centimeters and a variance of $0.02.$ If one shovel is randomly selected, what is the probability that its length is more than $150$ centimeters, but less than $150.5$ centimeters? You may assume that the lengths are independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ | $\\,0.8962\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.9115\\,$ | $\\,0.9131\\,$ | $\\,0.9147\\,$ | $\\,0.9162\\,$ | $\\,0.9177\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9265\\,$ | $\\,0.9279\\,$ | $\\,0.9292\\,$ | $\\,0.9306\\,$ | $\\,0.9319\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ denote the length of a handle, and let $Y$ denote the length of a blade. We want to find \n\n$$\nP(150<X+Y<150.5).\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables such that $X∼N(120,0.14)$ and $Y∼N(30,0.02)$, then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+Y & ∼N(120+30,0.14+0.02) \\\\  & ∼N(150,0.16).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variable $X+Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =150$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{0.16}=0.4.$\n\nIn order to find $P(150<X+Y<150.5),$ we convert $X+Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(150<X+Y<150.5) & =P(\\frac{150-150}{0.4}<Z<\\frac{150.5-150}{0.4}) \\\\  & ≈P(0<Z<1.25) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.25)-P(Z\\le 0) \\\\  & =Φ(1.25)-Φ(0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.25) & ≈0.8944,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0) & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(150<X+Y<150.5) & ≈Φ(1.25)-Φ(0) \\\\  & ≈0.8944-0.5 \\\\  & ≈0.3944.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that the probability that the length of a randomly selected shovel is more than $150$ centimeters, but less than $150.5$ centimeters is $0.3944.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb070c91-e2b2-5f1b-b37c-ab7d04905344"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb070c91-e2b2-5f1b-b37c-ab7d04905344" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb070c91-e2b2-5f1b-b37c-ab7d04905344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-912af71c-ec6c-5acf-a218-4c537f9cb75e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-912af71c-ec6c-5acf-a218-4c537f9cb75e" "answer-bca9eba0-cb3e-5af7-8eb5-bc98388caaf4" "answer-ac32782d-5d6e-552b-9ecc-ae443cf9c2be" "answer-edf7bc56-279f-5326-8543-b3671134dc41" "answer-2011937d-5a96-5735-baa1-c9d00e438e53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-912af71c-ec6c-5acf-a218-4c537f9cb75e" :answer/id #uuid "912af71c-ec6c-5acf-a218-4c537f9cb75e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3944" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bca9eba0-cb3e-5af7-8eb5-bc98388caaf4" :answer/id #uuid "bca9eba0-cb3e-5af7-8eb5-bc98388caaf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3980" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac32782d-5d6e-552b-9ecc-ae443cf9c2be" :answer/id #uuid "ac32782d-5d6e-552b-9ecc-ae443cf9c2be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4015" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-edf7bc56-279f-5326-8543-b3671134dc41" :answer/id #uuid "edf7bc56-279f-5326-8543-b3671134dc41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4131" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2011937d-5a96-5735-baa1-c9d00e438e53" :answer/id #uuid "2011937d-5a96-5735-baa1-c9d00e438e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4292" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c53663ac-ef5b-58bc-a1be-8cea3868fa2f" :question/id #uuid "c53663ac-ef5b-58bc-a1be-8cea3868fa2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-175410" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1}∼N(-3,1)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(1,2)$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+3{X}_{2} & ∼N(1\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 1,{1}^{2}\\cdot 1+{3}^{2}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & ∼N(0,19).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y∼N(0,19).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9fffc01b-d9f2-5f94-b352-b2003ad83619"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9fffc01b-d9f2-5f94-b352-b2003ad83619" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fffc01b-d9f2-5f94-b352-b2003ad83619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4186d1e-6606-5fe8-9ade-023864d3dde7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4186d1e-6606-5fe8-9ade-023864d3dde7" "answer-69890d9b-b5ce-57f5-9e6b-f58c9ce8bd33" "answer-41d541ba-49ec-5748-874b-c3423e6862f8" "answer-dc202adc-0608-5335-955f-0d38c624c45c" "answer-8012c74a-5d13-52a6-a453-e6796e086a62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4186d1e-6606-5fe8-9ade-023864d3dde7" :answer/id #uuid "b4186d1e-6606-5fe8-9ade-023864d3dde7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y∼N(0,19)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69890d9b-b5ce-57f5-9e6b-f58c9ce8bd33" :answer/id #uuid "69890d9b-b5ce-57f5-9e6b-f58c9ce8bd33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y∼N(0,36)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41d541ba-49ec-5748-874b-c3423e6862f8" :answer/id #uuid "41d541ba-49ec-5748-874b-c3423e6862f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y∼N(0,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc202adc-0608-5335-955f-0d38c624c45c" :answer/id #uuid "dc202adc-0608-5335-955f-0d38c624c45c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Y∼N(2,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8012c74a-5d13-52a6-a453-e6796e086a62" :answer/id #uuid "8012c74a-5d13-52a6-a453-e6796e086a62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Not enough information to determine the answer" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-77b5c58d-d4ec-5f66-9f2a-e4e55aab433c" :activity/id #uuid "77b5c58d-d4ec-5f66-9f2a-e4e55aab433c" :activity/title "Combining Two Normally Distributed Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049812 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-0526a648-ee54-5a70-b790-abd5fc388aa7" "step-a6c520d3-89e0-5390-82da-a20a42247402" "step-e71a59e7-528e-5195-bc2d-e6704ffb5651" "step-09e477d4-799c-59d3-9b5b-d55710b82507" "step-dad6d94b-b8a2-50a2-a3b8-ab747acac997"] :activity/first-step "step-0526a648-ee54-5a70-b790-abd5fc388aa7" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-0526a648-ee54-5a70-b790-abd5fc388aa7" :step/id #uuid "0526a648-ee54-5a70-b790-abd5fc388aa7" :step/content 17592186162271 :step/next "step-a6c520d3-89e0-5390-82da-a20a42247402" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a6c520d3-89e0-5390-82da-a20a42247402" :step/id #uuid "a6c520d3-89e0-5390-82da-a20a42247402" :step/content "question-65fa3d9f-f374-57d7-bfef-bf8f42da2e6e" :step/next "step-e71a59e7-528e-5195-bc2d-e6704ffb5651" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e71a59e7-528e-5195-bc2d-e6704ffb5651" :step/id #uuid "e71a59e7-528e-5195-bc2d-e6704ffb5651" :step/content "question-9dd9198d-6665-5e5e-bf17-48bb8a7b15be" :step/next "step-09e477d4-799c-59d3-9b5b-d55710b82507" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-09e477d4-799c-59d3-9b5b-d55710b82507" :step/id #uuid "09e477d4-799c-59d3-9b5b-d55710b82507" :step/content "question-666db65e-d2dd-5df6-aa61-3e935a25f26e" :step/next "step-dad6d94b-b8a2-50a2-a3b8-ab747acac997" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dad6d94b-b8a2-50a2-a3b8-ab747acac997" :step/id #uuid "dad6d94b-b8a2-50a2-a3b8-ab747acac997" :step/content "question-c53663ac-ef5b-58bc-a1be-8cea3868fa2f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167248 :question/answer-fields 17592186164595] [:db/retract 17592186167248 :question/answer-fields 17592186164598] [:db/retract 17592186167248 :question/answer-fields 17592186164605] {:db/id 17592186167248 :question/problem "![](images/71/718df02f2d0c2f01cc4a02a40da120178afe0f436bbf38cd5a8d249d87b5d1c9.png)\n\nConsider the phase portrait above showing a solution of a Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-6y+2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x=x(t),y=y(t),$ and $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are positive constants.\n\nSelect the options below that best describe the dynamics of the system from point $A$ to point $B$ on the solution.\n\n$\\,$\nThe trajectory \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$\nThe number of prey {{field-3}} and the number of predators {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The Lotka-Volterra predator-prey model is given by\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=ax-bxy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-cy+dxy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,d$ are positive real constants. Here, $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements:\n\n- The trajectory $\\text{circles around}$ $\\text{the nonzero equilibrium}.$\n\n- From $A$ to $B,$ the number of prey $\\text{decreases}$ and the number of predators $\\text{increases}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186370186 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=-2x+3xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=7y-5xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey. Find the nonzero equilibrium of the model.\n\n$(${{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3xy=0 \\\\ 7y-5xy=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+3xy & =0 \\\\ x(-2+3y) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x=0$ or $y=\\frac{2}{3}.$ We consider both cases separately.\n\n- If $x=0,$ substituting it into the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y-5(0)y=0\\,⇒\\,y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, one equilibrium is $(0,0).$\n\n- If $y=\\frac{2}{3},$ substituting it into the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y-5xy & =0 \\\\ y(7-5x) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}(7-5x) & =0 \\\\ 7-5x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(\\frac{7}{5},\\frac{2}{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero equilibrium of the model is\n$(\\frac{7}{5},\\frac{2}{3}).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ec6a2eb-63e4-55a4-849b-ba0f89289e7d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ec6a2eb-63e4-55a4-849b-ba0f89289e7d" :question/id #uuid "9ec6a2eb-63e4-55a4-849b-ba0f89289e7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335018" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=-0.5x+0.5xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=y-5xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the predators and $y=y(t)$ represents the prey. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0.2,\\,1]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is\n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote ${f}_{1}(x,y)=-0.5x+0.5xy$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=y-5xy.$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-0.5x+0.5xy)=-0.5+0.5y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-0.5x+0.5xy)=0.5x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-5xy)=-5y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-5xy)=1-5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the Jacobian matrix is\n\n$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}-0.5+0.5y & 0.5x \\\\ -5y & 1-5x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\nJ({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}-0.5+0.5(1) & 0.5(0.2) \\\\ -5(1) & 1-5(0.2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0.1 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix, we write down the characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0.1 \\\\ -5 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-(-5)\\cdot 0.1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+0.5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation, we get the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=\\pm 0.5\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}.$ Since the eigenvalues are purely imaginary, our equilibrium is $\\text{a stable}$ $\\text{center}.$\n\n**Note:**\nFor the Lotka-Volterra model (as in this problem), it is safe to classify the nonzero equilibrium as a center when the linearization has purely imaginary eigenvalues. \n\n**Watch out!** \nIn contrast, for a general nonlinear system, the Jacobian test alone is inconclusive (additional analysis is required to determine whether the equilibrium is a true center or a spiral sink/source)." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76ffae76-26cc-5fc1-83ca-c7cd4df10103" "answer-field-04f7fce6-8db2-54b1-a219-ef981e8d8a0a" "answer-field-1df273f0-6360-5b3c-996f-84b52a0c2e4e" "answer-field-f7b73c3c-e37c-5ccd-b7bc-8a667a8d5029" "answer-field-0c9a3e35-07ce-5a6f-a791-beaf98dca1d9" "answer-field-3d5cf5f8-e409-5012-a1e4-61c220034dce" "answer-field-f74ac2ca-c624-58dd-9d66-708a048e2455"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76ffae76-26cc-5fc1-83ca-c7cd4df10103" :answer-field/id #uuid "76ffae76-26cc-5fc1-83ca-c7cd4df10103" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-74e49c08-fa40-5af5-8b36-283e9d1a618b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d06dde3-0cc6-5fef-aa3c-fb368c5d1065" "answer-74e49c08-fa40-5af5-8b36-283e9